{
  "summary": "The current codebase still contains all previously reported open findings; three of the earlier issues have been resolved (CSV injection, PDF HTML injection, and the uuid vulnerability). No critical or high‑severity new findings were discovered except for a newly identified high‑severity issue: the optional biometric app‑lock is only verified on initial launch and not on app resume, allowing an attacker to bypass the lock after the app is backgrounded. All other findings remain unchanged and un‑fixed.",
  "previous": [
    {
      "id": "high-deps-braces-2026-93687",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "high",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; dependency vulnerability persists"
    },
    {
      "id": "high-deps-node-forge-2026-85393",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "high",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; dependency vulnerability persists"
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-backup-passphrase-policy",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; backup UI accepts any non‑empty passphrase"
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-web-key-storage",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; key persisted in localStorage in web fallback"
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-temp-backup-file-deletion",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; temporary backup file is never deleted"
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-input-validation-numeric",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; numeric fields lack validation"
    },
    {
      "id": "deployment-csp-header",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; web build lacks a CSP header/meta tag"
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-image-size-validation-2026-00001",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; photo picker accepts arbitrarily large images"
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-key-persistence-after-data-delete",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; encryption key remains after \"Delete all data\""
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-deps-sprintf-js-2026-97058",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; transitive sprintf-js vulnerability"
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-record-count-limit",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; no caps on number of records"
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-export-throttling",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "no change – still open; exports can be invoked repeatedly without limits"
    },
    {
      "id": "high-csv-injection",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "high",
      "severity_change_reason": "fixed – CSV export now sanitises leading =,+,-,@ and quotes fields"
    },
    {
      "id": "high-pdf-html-injection",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "high",
      "severity_change_reason": "fixed – HTML for PDF is escaped via htmlEscape before rendering"
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-deps-uuid-2026-41907",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "fixed – uuid upgraded to a safe version (>=13.0.1)"
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "app-lock-resume-bypass",
      "severity": "high",
      "where": "code",
      "file": "src/App.tsx",
      "issue": "The optional biometric/app‑lock is only evaluated once when the app first becomes ready. If the user backgrounds the app and later returns, the lock is not re‑checked, allowing any person with physical access to the device to view the unlocked UI and sensitive data without re‑authenticating.",
      "fix": "Add an AppState listener (or use @react-native-community/hooks) that triggers the biometric authentication whenever the app transitions to the foreground while `appLockEnabled` is true. On failed authentication, reset the UI to a locked state (e.g., set `locked` to true and render the loading spinner or a lock screen). Ensure the lock state persists across navigation and is cleared only after successful authentication."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "Overall the UI implements the primary flow and most screens/states described in DESIGN.md, and the headless audits (axe, Lighthouse, layout) report no major accessibility violations. However a few gaps were found: missing or incomplete error/loading UI for the policy gate, some accessibility details (ARIA labels on spinners, focus‑visible outlines, role/label on navigation and FABs) are not fully covered, a handful of components still use hard‑coded colors/sizes instead of the design tokens, and the mini‑FABs violate the 44 × 44 dp touch‑target requirement. These issues can affect users with assistive technologies and break the high‑severity bar for polish, so they should be addressed before release.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The PolicyGate UI only implements the default agreement state; the loading spinner screen and the error view with a Retry button (required for the Loading and Error states) are missing.",
      "fix": "Add a full‑screen `<ActivityIndicator>` with an accessible label \"Checking policy version…\" for the loading state, and an error view that displays the message \"Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.\" with a `<PrimaryButton>` labelled \"Retry\" that re‑attempts storing the acceptance."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BottomTabBar.tsx",
      "issue": "The bottom navigation component lacks an explicit `accessibilityRole=\"navigation\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Bottom navigation\"`, which means screen readers do not announce it as a landmark.",
      "fix": "Wrap the `BottomNavigation` in a container with `accessibilityRole=\"navigation\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Bottom navigation\"`, or pass these props directly to the component."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "The large FAB and the mini‑FABs only set `accessibilityLabel` on the large FAB; the mini‑FABs for \"Receipt\" and \"Mileage\" lack `accessibilityLabel`/`accessibilityHint`, making them invisible to screen readers.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Add receipt\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Add mileage\"` (or appropriate hints) to each mini‑FAB, and ensure they also have `accessibilityRole=\"button\"`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus‑visible styling is not applied on web; when the button receives keyboard focus there is no visible outline, violating WCAG 2.1 success criterion 2.4.7.",
      "fix": "Add a 2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline` when the button is in `:focus-visible` state (or use React Native Paper's `theme` to customize `rippleColor`/`borderWidth` for focus)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/MiniFAB.tsx",
      "issue": "Mini‑FABs are sized 40 × 40 dp, which is below the required 44 × 44 dp touch target, reducing tappable area for many users.",
      "fix": "Increase the hit‑area to at least 44 × 44 dp by adding transparent padding around the icon or using `TouchableRipple` with a larger `style` while keeping the visual size at 40 × 40 dp."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "The global screen container sets padding via a literal `paddingHorizontal: 16` and width via `maxWidth: 420` directly in the style object, bypassing the design tokens (`theme.spacing` and `theme.roundness`).",
      "fix": "Replace hard‑coded values with token references, e.g., `paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing * 2` and `maxWidth: 420` should be derived from a token or a constant that lives in `theme.ts`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The illustration image uses a hard‑coded color filter (`tintColor: '#6F6F6F'`) instead of the `placeholder` token from the design palette.",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded hex with `theme.colors.placeholder` or the CSS custom property `var(--color-placeholder)`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ReceiptCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Card elevation is set to `elevation={2}` directly; the spec defines elevation level1 in the theme (`elevation.level1`).",
      "fix": "Use `elevation={theme.elevation.level1.elevation}` and apply the matching shadow opacity from the token."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ActivityIndicator.tsx",
      "issue": "The spinner components do not have an `accessibilityLabel` describing their purpose (e.g., \"Loading receipts…\").",
      "fix": "Pass `accessibilityLabel` with the appropriate copy for each loading state, matching the text defined in the design table."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/HelperText.tsx",
      "issue": "Error `HelperText` components are rendered without `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"polite\"` or `role=\"alert\"`, which can prevent screen readers from announcing validation messages promptly.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"polite\"` and `role=\"alert\"` to the `HelperText` component when `type=\"error\"`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields use generic `keyboardType` values but do not set `autoCompleteType` (e.g., `autocomplete=\"off\"` for amount) or `textContentType` for better autofill on supported platforms.",
      "fix": "Add appropriate `autoComplete`/`textContentType` props: `keyboardType=\"numeric\"` and `autoComplete=\"transaction-amount\"` for amount, `autoComplete=\"username\"` etc., where relevant."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The passphrase fields do not enforce or communicate the required minimum length/complexity (the UI accepts any non‑empty string).",
      "fix": "Implement validation that requires at least 8 characters and three of four character classes, display a `HelperText` error, and keep the \"Create backup\" button disabled until the policy is satisfied."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "score": 8,
  "summary": "A polished, modern onboarding screen with clear visual hierarchy and a single primary action. Typography is well-scaled and readable. Spacing and alignment are consistent and generous. The design feels professional and would not look out of place in a commercial app. Minor improvements could enhance the visual hierarchy and form interaction.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "viewport": "both",
      "issue": "The primary action button is disabled until the checkbox is checked, which is correct behavior, but the button's disabled state is not visually distinct enough to clearly communicate its state to users.",
      "fix": "Apply a more pronounced disabled state to the button — e.g., lighter color, opacity, or subtle border styling — to make it unmistakably inactive until the checkbox is checked."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "viewport": "both",
      "issue": "The checkbox is positioned slightly too far to the left relative to its label, creating an asymmetrical layout that breaks the visual alignment of the form group.",
      "fix": "Center-align the checkbox and its label within the form group for better visual balance and consistency with common form patterns."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "viewport": "both",
      "issue": "The 'Tick the box to continue' instruction is positioned below the button, which is counterintuitive. Users might not immediately understand that the instruction refers to the checkbox above it.",
      "fix": "Move the instruction directly under the checkbox, aligned with it, to clearly associate it with the required action."
    }
  ]
}

