{
  "summary": "The implementation follows the design spec closely – the primary flow was exercised on both phone and desktop, all screens render, and axe reported zero accessibility violations. The visual hierarchy, theming and layout are generally on‑point. However, a handful of serious UX/accessibility gaps were found: the mini‑FABs are smaller than the 44 × 44 dp touch‑target guideline, the PolicyGate error screen lacks a functional Retry button, the backup passphrase screen does not enforce the required length/complexity, some forms allow submission before validation passes, and focus‑visible outlines are missing on key interactive components. There are also several medium‑severity inconsistencies such as missing accessibility labels on image‑pickers and empty‑state illustrations, hard‑coded spacing values instead of design‑token references, and missing rate‑limiting on export actions. These issues should be addressed before the product is released.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/MiniFAB.tsx",
      "issue": "Mini‑FAB touch area is 40 × 40 dp, below the required 44 × 44 dp minimum for accessible touch targets, making it hard to tap on mobile devices.",
      "fix": "Wrap the 40 × 40 visual button in an invisible hit‑area (e.g., padding or a transparent TouchableOpacity) so the total touchable region is at least 44 × 44 dp while keeping the visual size unchanged."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Error view does not include a visible \"Retry\" button (or the button does not trigger the policy‑gate retry logic), leaving the user stuck when storage fails.",
      "fix": "Add a PrimaryButton labeled \"Retry\" that re‑executes the store‑acceptance step and ensure it matches the copy \"Retry\" as defined in DESIGN.md."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup passphrase field only checks for non‑empty input; it does not enforce the required minimum of 8 characters or character‑class complexity, contradicting the spec.",
      "fix": "Implement validation that requires ≥8 characters and at least three of the four character classes (uppercase, lowercase, digit, symbol). Disable the \"Create backup\" button until the rule passes and show a HelperText error when it does not."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Save receipt button can be pressed while required fields are invalid; only a Snackbar error is shown after the failed save.",
      "fix": "Add client‑side validation that disables the Save button until all mandatory fields are valid. Show per‑field HelperText errors and focus the first invalid field on submit."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Same issue as ReceiptEntryScreen – Save mileage button is enabled before validation passes.",
      "fix": "Mirror the validation logic from ReceiptEntryScreen: disable Save until amount, date, and purpose fields are valid, display HelperText errors, and focus the first invalid field."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "No visible focus outline on web; keyboard navigation does not give a clear indication of which button is focused.",
      "fix": "Add a style rule that applies a 2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline` when the button receives focus (e.g., `:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-outline); }`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Photo picker button in ReceiptEntryScreen lacks an `accessibilityLabel`, causing screen‑reader users to miss the control.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Add photo\"` to the photo‑picker button and, when a photo is present, `accessibilityLabel=\"Remove photo\"` to the remove icon."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "Illustration image does not have an `accessibilityLabel` (alt text), violating the accessible‑image guideline.",
      "fix": "Pass a meaningful `accessibilityLabel` like \"Empty state illustration\" to the `<Image>` component inside EmptyState."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BottomTabBar.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom navigation lacks `role=\"navigation\"` and `aria-label` on the component, which can reduce screen‑reader discoverability.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"navigation\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Bottom navigation\"` (or `aria-label` on web) to the BottomTabBar container."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Horizontal padding is hard‑coded as `paddingHorizontal: 16` instead of using `theme.spacing` token, breaking the token‑driven design system.",
      "fix": "Replace the literal `16` with `theme.spacing * 2` (or a utility `space(2)`) so spacing is derived from the design token."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export buttons can be tapped repeatedly, spawning multiple async export jobs; no throttling or disabled state while an export is in progress.",
      "fix": "Disable both Export CSV and Export PDF buttons while `isGenerating` is true and re‑enable after the share completes; optionally debounce button taps with a 5‑second interval."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Card.tsx",
      "issue": "Card components use hard‑coded `borderRadius: 8` and `marginBottom: 16` values instead of the `theme.roundness` and `theme.spacing` tokens.",
      "fix": "Replace the literal numbers with `theme.roundness` and `theme.spacing * 2` respectively to keep styles token‑consistent."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Error view shows only a \"Retry\" button but the copy reads \"Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.\" – the UI does not support pull‑to‑refresh, causing a mismatch between copy and behavior.",
      "fix": "Either implement a pull‑to‑refresh gesture on the ScrollView and keep the copy, or change the copy to \"Failed to load data. Tap Retry to try again.\" to match the UI."
    }
  ]
}

