{
  "summary": "Overall the UI matches the DESIGN.md specification and passes automated accessibility (axe) and Lighthouse (A11y 98, Best Practices 100) checks. All screens and primary states exist and navigation works. However, there are a handful of design‑token mismatches, missing validation/enforcement on the backup passphrase, a few copy inaccuracies, and some interaction‑state/focus styling gaps that need to be addressed to bring the product to a truly polished level.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Empty‑state description still reads “Tap the + button to add your first receipt.” instead of the mileage‑specific copy “Tap the + button to log your first mileage entry.”",
      "fix": "Update the EmptyState component props for MileageScreen to use the correct title/description/copy as defined in DESIGN.md."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Passphrase validation only checks for matching confirm field; it does not enforce the required minimum length of 8 characters (or any complexity rules) which the design and security review call for.",
      "fix": "Add validation that the passphrase is ≥ 8 characters (and optionally enforce three of four character classes). Disable the “Create backup” button until the policy is satisfied and show a HelperText error message matching the design."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/MiniFAB.tsx",
      "issue": "MiniFAB uses the default React‑Native‑Paper `FAB` with no explicit color prop, resulting in the primary accent color being applied instead of the secondary teal defined in the design tokens.",
      "fix": "Pass `color={theme.colors.onSecondary}` and `style={{ backgroundColor: theme.colors.secondary }}` (or use a custom `mode=\"secondary\"` implementation) so that the MiniFAB background uses `secondary` and the icon uses `onSecondary` as specified."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus-visible outline (2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline`) is not implemented for web, so keyboard users cannot see a clear focus indicator on the button.",
      "fix": "Add a `:focus-visible` CSS rule (or React Native Web style) that applies a 2 dp outline with `theme.colors.outline` to the button when focused."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Accept button is not disabled until the policy checkbox is checked; the button is always enabled, allowing users to bypass agreement.",
      "fix": "Bind the `disabled` prop of the Accept button to the checkbox state, matching the spec where the button is disabled until the user checks the agreement."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing error handling UI for settings loading failure – the spec calls for a Snackbar error, but the screen only logs errors without showing a Snackbar.",
      "fix": "Wrap the settings fetch in a try/catch and on error display a `Snackbar` with the message “Unable to load settings.” matching the design."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen container applies padding via a hard‑coded value (`padding: 16`) instead of using the design token `theme.spacing * 2`.",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded padding with `style={{ paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing * 2 }}` to stay consistent with the token system."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields lack `autoComplete` props (e.g., `autocomplete=\"off\"` for notes, `autocomplete=\"shipping address-line1\"` is not set for amount). While not a blocker, adding appropriate autocomplete attributes improves UX.",
      "fix": "Add relevant `autoComplete` attributes based on field purpose (numeric fields `autocomplete=\"off\"`, date field `autocomplete=\"bday\"` etc.) ensuring they align with the design’s best practice."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ExportButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Export buttons do not show a loading spinner overlay with the copy “Generating export…”; they only show the spinner without the accompanying text.",
      "fix": "When `loading` is true, render a full‑screen overlay containing an `ActivityIndicator` and a `<Text>` element with the exact copy “Generating export…” as defined in DESIGN.md."
