{
  "summary": "The screen reads as an unstyled list: there is no way to add a receipt (the spec's + FAB is missing), the tab bar labels are clipped by the safe area, and the ReceiptCard has no typographic hierarchy — amount, meta and note are all near-equal weight with 'Date:'/'Category:' prefixes and a bare text 'Expense' tag. Fixing the card component, the tab bar and adding the FAB in shared code lifts Receipts, Mileage and Dashboard at once.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Add-receipt FAB (missing)",
      "issue": "The primary action for this screen is absent; spec copy ('Tap the + button to add your first receipt') and the primary flow both rely on a FAB, so the loaded list is a dead end.",
      "fix": "Add Paper <FAB icon=\"plus\" label=\"Add receipt\" onPress={...} /> positioned absolute bottom-right, right: 16, bottom: 16 + bottom tab bar height (use useBottomTabBarHeight()), and give the FlatList contentContainerStyle paddingBottom: 96 so the last card is never covered. Put this in a shared src/components/ui/ScreenFab.tsx used by Receipts, Mileage and Dashboard.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Bottom tab bar (BottomNavigation / Tab.Navigator)",
      "issue": "At 390x844 the labels 'Dashboard / Receipts / Mileage / Settings' are cut off at the bottom edge — the bar has no safe-area inset and insufficient height.",
      "fix": "In the navigator's screenOptions set tabBarStyle={{ height: 56 + insets.bottom, paddingTop: 8, paddingBottom: insets.bottom || 8, backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface, borderTopColor: theme.colors.outlineVariant }} using useSafeAreaInsets(), and tabBarLabelStyle={{ fontSize: 12, lineHeight: 16 }}. Also set tabBarActiveTintColor: theme.colors.primary and tabBarInactiveTintColor: theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant so icons and labels share one color (today icons and labels are mismatched teal/blue).",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "ReceiptCard — typography hierarchy",
      "issue": "Amount, date, category and note are all rendered at roughly the same size/weight, so the card has no scan order and reads as a form dump; 'Date:' and 'Category:' label prefixes add noise.",
      "fix": "In src/components/ui/ReceiptCard.tsx: amount Text variant=\"titleLarge\" color onSurface; drop the 'Date:'/'Category:' prefixes and render one meta line '2026-10-10 · Supplies' as Text variant=\"bodySmall\" color onSurfaceVariant with marginTop 4; note as Text variant=\"bodyMedium\" color onSurfaceVariant numberOfLines={2} with marginTop 8.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "ReceiptCard — 'Expense' type indicator",
      "issue": "The type is plain teal text that looks like a tappable link and competes with the amount.",
      "fix": "Replace with <Chip compact mode=\"flat\" textStyle={{fontSize:12}}> using theme.colors.secondaryContainer / onSecondaryContainer for Expense and errorContainer/onErrorContainer (or tertiaryContainer) for Income, aligned right in the same flexDirection:'row', justifyContent:'space-between', alignItems:'center' header row as the amount.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Screen header 'Receipts'",
      "issue": "Oversized display-size title with ~48px of ad-hoc top padding and no shared structure, so headers will drift between screens; on desktop it sits centered above a narrow column.",
      "fix": "Create src/components/ui/ScreenHeader.tsx rendering <Text variant=\"headlineMedium\"> inside a View with paddingHorizontal: 16, paddingTop: 8, paddingBottom: 16, placed under SafeAreaView edges={['top']}; use it on all four tabs so list content starts 16px below the title.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "List layout / card spacing and width",
      "issue": "Card has no separator rhythm defined for multiple items, and on desktop the 1280px canvas leaves one small card floating in a huge empty area.",
      "fix": "FlatList: contentContainerStyle={{ paddingHorizontal: 16, paddingTop: 8, gap: 12, maxWidth: 720, width: '100%', alignSelf: 'center' }} and remove per-card margins; give Card mode=\"elevated\" elevation={1} with borderRadius 16 from theme.roundness and Card.Content padding 16.",
      "shared": true
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "The form reads as a stack of generic boxes: the screen title is duplicated, the photo step looks like a text link instead of a capture target, field heights and gaps are irregular, and the primary action floats mid-screen. Fixing input/spacing rules in a shared FormField + a sticky action footer in the theme will carry over to the mileage and settings forms.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Screen heading 'Add receipt' (below the Appbar)",
      "issue": "The title is printed twice — once in the Appbar and again as a headline inside the scroll view — wasting ~90px above the fold and making the Appbar look decorative.",
      "fix": "Delete the in-page <Text variant=\"headlineLarge\">Add receipt</Text>. Keep only <Appbar.Header mode=\"small\"> with the back action and title=\"Add receipt\" (titleLarge). Set the ScrollView contentContainerStyle to { padding: 16, paddingTop: 16, paddingBottom: 24 } so the photo picker starts right under the Appbar.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "'Add photo' control",
      "issue": "An outlined Button with blue text reads as a link and gives no sense of what gets captured; it is also separated from the fields by a 72px orphan gap.",
      "fix": "Replace with a shared <PhotoPicker/>: Pressable <Surface mode=\"flat\"> height 120, borderRadius 12, backgroundColor theme.colors.surfaceVariant, borderWidth 1 borderColor theme.colors.outlineVariant, centered column with <Icon source=\"camera-plus\" size={28} color={colors.onSurfaceVariant}/>, gap 8, Text variant=\"labelLarge\" 'Add photo' and variant=\"bodySmall\" 'Optional' in onSurfaceVariant. When a photo exists, render the image at the same size with a small 'Replace'/'Remove' icon button overlay. marginBottom 24.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Text inputs (Amount, Date, Category, Notes)",
      "issue": "Fields are ~80px tall with the label vertically centered as a placeholder, and the gaps between them are inconsistent (72 / 40 / 40 / 8 / 24px), so the form has no rhythm and no visible floating-label behaviour.",
      "fix": "Create src/components/ui/FormField.tsx wrapping <TextInput mode=\"outlined\" dense={false} style={{ marginBottom: 0 }} outlineStyle={{ borderRadius: 12 }} /> at Paper's default 56px height (Notes: multiline numberOfLines={3}, ~96px) plus a always-reserved <HelperText type=\"error\" visible={!!error} padding=\"none\"> slot. Stack all fields in a <View style={{ gap: 16 }}> and use a single 24px gap before the Type group and before the save area.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "'Save receipt' button",
      "issue": "The primary action sits mid-page with ~440px of dead space below it, and in the disabled state it is a flat grey slab with no hint of what is missing.",
      "fix": "Move it into a shared <FormFooter/>: <Surface elevation={2} style={{ padding: 16, paddingBottom: 16 + insets.bottom }}> pinned to the bottom of the screen, containing <Button mode=\"contained\" style={{ width: '100%' }} contentStyle={{ height: 48 }} labelStyle={theme.fonts.labelLarge} disabled={!valid} loading={saving}>Save receipt</Button>. Add <HelperText type=\"info\"> 'Enter an amount and date to save' above the button while disabled.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Type selector (Expense / Income)",
      "issue": "The group label is small teal text that conflicts with the grey field labels, and the selected segment uses a flat mint fill with no check icon, so it doesn't read as the same control family as the inputs.",
      "fix": "Label: <Text variant=\"labelLarge\" style={{ color: colors.onSurfaceVariant, marginBottom: 8 }}>Type</Text>. Control: Paper <SegmentedButtons value density=\"regular\" buttons={[{value:'expense',label:'Expense',icon:'arrow-down',showSelectedCheck:true},{value:'income',label:'Income',icon:'arrow-up',showSelectedCheck:true}]} /> so the selection uses secondaryContainer + checkmark from the theme rather than a custom fill.",
      "shared": false
    },
    {
      "element": "Category field",
      "issue": "Category is rendered as a free-text input identical to Amount/Notes, but the spec treats it as a fixed list — users can't tell it opens a picker.",
      "fix": "Render as a select: <TextInput mode=\"outlined\" editable={false} showSoftInputOnFocus={false} right={<TextInput.Icon icon=\"menu-down\" />} onPressIn={openMenu} /> anchored to a Paper <Menu> of categories (same 56px height and 12px radius as other fields).",
      "shared": false
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "The dashboard reads as a stack of unstyled boxes with two overlapping overlays: the Snackbar sits mid‑screen on top of a receipt card and the two stacked extended FABs, and the tab bar labels are clipped by the home‑indicator area. Fixing the overlay/safe‑area layer, collapsing the two FABs into one Paper FAB.Group, tightening the recent‑activity card, and unifying the teal/blue color use in the theme would make the screen feel designed rather than assembled.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Snackbar (\"Receipt saved\")",
      "issue": "Rendered at a fixed mid‑screen offset, covering the second receipt card and crossing the FABs; it also spans edge‑to‑edge with no radius, which looks like an error banner.",
      "fix": "Move the Snackbar into a shared <AppSnackbar> rendered in a Portal at the root: wrapperStyle={{ bottom: insets.bottom + 72 }} (clears the 64dp tab bar), style={{ marginHorizontal: 16, borderRadius: 8 }}, duration={3000}, and pass the FAB a `visible`-driven translateY of -56 (or use Paper's FAB `visible`/snackbar anchor pattern) so nothing overlaps.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Bottom tab bar",
      "issue": "Labels \"Dashboard / Receipts / Mileage / Settings\" are cut off at the phone's bottom edge — the bar has no safe‑area padding and too little height.",
      "fix": "In the shared tab navigator options set height: 64 + insets.bottom (useSafeAreaInsets), paddingBottom: insets.bottom + 8, paddingTop: 8, tabBarLabelStyle = theme.fonts.labelMedium (12/16, no clipping), icon size 24, and tabBarActiveTintColor: theme.colors.primary / inactive: theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "\"Add receipt\" / \"Add mileage\" extended FABs",
      "issue": "Two full‑width-ish extended FABs stacked and misaligned on the right, sitting on top of list content and the snackbar — the spec calls for one FAB with mini‑FAB choices.",
      "fix": "Replace with Paper <FAB.Group open={open} icon={open ? 'close' : 'plus'} actions={[{icon:'receipt', label:'Add receipt'},{icon:'car', label:'Add mileage'}]} /> positioned bottom‑right with fabStyle={{ marginRight: 16, marginBottom: insets.bottom + 16 }}, and add paddingBottom: 96 to the dashboard ScrollView contentContainerStyle so the last card is never obscured.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Recent‑activity entry card (ReceiptCard)",
      "issue": "Four stacked left‑aligned lines with raw \"Date:\"/\"Category:\" prefixes and an ISO date make the card ~250px tall and visually noisy; the type label is plain teal text, not a recognizable affordance.",
      "fix": "Restructure the shared card to Card.Content with: row 1 = amount (titleLarge, onSurface) + Paper <Chip compact mode=\"flat\"> for Expense/Income; row 2 = 'Oct 10, 2026 · Supplies' (bodyMedium, onSurfaceVariant); row 3 = note (bodySmall, onSurfaceVariant). Padding 16, gap 4, card marginBottom 12, mode=\"outlined\" with theme.colors.outlineVariant instead of the current drop shadow.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Theme colors (teal labels vs blue FAB/tab icons)",
      "issue": "Two unrelated accent hues are used — teal/green for card labels and the \"Expense\" tag, blue for FABs and active tab — so nothing reads as the brand color.",
      "fix": "In src/theme.ts keep one primary (the blue, e.g. #0B63B3) used for FAB, active tab and links; change SummaryCard labels and the type tag to theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant / tertiary‑container chip. Nothing in the content area should use raw teal text.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Screen title \"Dashboard\" and \"Recent activity\" heading",
      "issue": "The title is oversized (~40px displaySmall) eating a third of the first viewport, while the section heading is the same weight as body copy, so hierarchy is flat.",
      "fix": "Create a shared <ScreenHeader> using Text variant=\"headlineMedium\" (28/36) with paddingHorizontal 16, paddingTop 16, paddingBottom 16; render section headings as Text variant=\"titleMedium\" with color onSurfaceVariant, marginTop 24, marginBottom 8. Apply the same 16px horizontal gutter to summary cards (currently 48px inset on phone).",
      "shared": true
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "The data is all there but the screen reads as unstyled: the tab bar labels are clipped by the missing safe-area inset, the snackbar and the two stacked 'Add' buttons cover the last activity card, and both the summary cards and activity rows use default body text with teal accents instead of a real MD3 hierarchy. The highest-leverage fixes are in the tab navigator, a shared SummaryCard/ActivityCard, and a shared screen container that caps width on desktop.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Bottom tab bar (Dashboard | Receipts | Mileage | Settings)",
      "issue": "Labels are cut off at the bottom edge on phone — the bar does not account for the safe-area inset, and its height is too small for icon + label.",
      "fix": "In the navigator options set tabBarStyle={{ height: 56 + insets.bottom, paddingTop: 8, paddingBottom: insets.bottom + 8, borderTopWidth: StyleSheet.hairlineWidth, borderTopColor: theme.colors.outlineVariant, backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface }} using useSafeAreaInsets(), and tabBarLabelStyle={{ fontSize: 12, lineHeight: 16, marginTop: 4 }}. Use theme.colors.primary for the active tint and theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant for inactive.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Add receipt / Add mileage buttons",
      "issue": "Two full-width-ish extended buttons float over the activity list as a permanent stack; the spec calls for a FAB that opens Receipt/Mileage mini-FABs, and the current stack hides card content.",
      "fix": "Replace with Paper's <FAB.Group open={open} icon={open ? 'close' : 'plus'} visible actions={[{icon:'receipt', label:'Add receipt'},{icon:'car', label:'Add mileage'}]} onStateChange={...} fabStyle={{ backgroundColor: theme.colors.primaryContainer }} /> positioned bottom-right with 16px margin and bottom offset = tabBarHeight + 16. FAB.Group supplies the scrim so the list is dimmed, not obscured.",
      "shared": false
    },
    {
      "element": "Snackbar 'Mileage saved'",
      "issue": "Snackbar spans edge-to-edge, sits mid-list on top of a card and collides with the action buttons; it has no inset or elevation separation.",
      "fix": "Render the Snackbar from a shared <SnackbarProvider> with wrapperStyle={{ bottom: tabBarHeight + fabHeight + 24, marginHorizontal: 16 }}, duration 3000, borderRadius 4, and theme.colors.inverseSurface background. Keep it above the FAB stack so neither overlaps list content.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "SummaryCard (Income / Expenses / Mileage deduction / Estimated tax)",
      "issue": "Label is teal (primary) and the same size as the value's neighbours, so the four cards read as links; values use a generic bold that is not a type ramp step, and cards use a heavy drop shadow on a grey background.",
      "fix": "In SummaryCard: label = <Text variant=\"labelMedium\" style={{color: theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant}}>, value = <Text variant=\"headlineSmall\" style={{color: theme.colors.onSurface}}> with 4px gap; Card mode=\"contained\" with backgroundColor theme.colors.surface, borderRadius 12, padding 16, elevation 0 plus 1px theme.colors.outlineVariant border. Grid gap 8 instead of the current uneven ~16/24.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Recent activity list item",
      "issue": "Each row prints 'Date: …' and 'Category: …' as raw body text in four stacked lines, making the card tall and low-contrast; the type ('Expense') is teal text, not a status affordance.",
      "fix": "Rebuild as a shared ActivityCard: row 1 = amount <Text variant=\"titleMedium\"> left, <Chip compact mode=\"flat\"> for 'Expense'/'Income' right using errorContainer/secondaryContainer; row 2 = <Text variant=\"bodySmall\" color=onSurfaceVariant> with 'Supplies · 2026-10-10' (drop the 'Date:'/'Category:' prefixes); row 3 = note in bodySmall, numberOfLines={1}. Card padding 16, vertical gap 8, 8px between cards.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Screen container / 'Recent activity' heading",
      "issue": "On desktop the content stretches to 1280px so summary cards become wide and empty, and the section heading is plain body text at the same weight as the cards.",
      "fix": "Add a shared <ScreenContainer> with contentContainerStyle={{ width:'100%', maxWidth: 840, alignSelf:'center', paddingHorizontal: 16, paddingBottom: tabBarHeight + 96 }} and use it on every screen; render the heading as <Text variant=\"titleMedium\"> with marginTop 24 / marginBottom 8.",
      "shared": true
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "The screen reads as a bare form: the page title duplicates the app bar, the supporting copy is mis-colored as a link, the passphrase fields behave like plain text inputs with no masking or reveal toggle, and the critical \"you cannot recover a lost passphrase\" warning is missing. The bottom tab bar also clips its labels on phone because it ignores the safe-area inset, and its active color is inconsistent — both are shared-component fixes that affect every screen.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Bottom tab bar (shared BottomNavigation / Tab.Navigator)",
      "issue": "Labels are vertically clipped at phone size (\"Dashboard\", \"Receipts\" cut in half) because the bar has a fixed height and no safe-area bottom inset.",
      "fix": "In the shared tab bar component use `const insets = useSafeAreaInsets()` and set `tabBarStyle={{ height: 56 + insets.bottom, paddingTop: 8, paddingBottom: 8 + insets.bottom }}` and `tabBarLabelStyle={{ ...theme.fonts.labelMedium, marginTop: 4 }}`. Remove any hard-coded height.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Page heading \"Create backup\" vs. Appbar title",
      "issue": "The same string is rendered twice (Appbar.Content and an in-body headlineLarge), wasting ~88px above the fold and creating a confusing double title.",
      "fix": "Delete the in-body `Text variant=\"headlineLarge\"`. Keep `Appbar.Header` with `Appbar.Content title=\"Create backup\"` and start the body with the supporting sentence at 24px top padding. Apply this rule in the shared ScreenScaffold so no screen repeats its app bar title.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Passphrase + Confirm passphrase TextInputs",
      "issue": "Values are not masked and there is no reveal control, no confirm helper text; the two fields are visually identical so the confirm field has no feedback affordance.",
      "fix": "Create shared `PassphraseInput` wrapping `<TextInput mode=\"outlined\" secureTextEntry={!visible} autoCapitalize=\"none\" autoCorrect={false} textContentType=\"newPassword\" right={<TextInput.Icon icon={visible ? 'eye-off' : 'eye'} onPress={toggle} accessibilityLabel=\"Show passphrase\" />} />` plus a persistent `<HelperText type=\"info\" visible>` slot. Use it for both fields; confirm helper: \"Re-enter the same passphrase\" and `type=\"error\"` \"Passphrases don't match\" on mismatch.",
      "shared": false
    },
    {
      "element": "Missing recovery warning",
      "issue": "Nothing tells the user the passphrase is unrecoverable — the highest-stakes fact on this screen.",
      "fix": "Insert between the Confirm field and the CTA a `<Card mode=\"contained\" style={{ backgroundColor: theme.colors.secondaryContainer, padding: 16, marginVertical: 24 }}>` with `icon=\"alert-circle-outline\"` (24px, colors.onSecondaryContainer) and `Text variant=\"bodySmall\"`: \"If you lose this passphrase, the backup file cannot be restored. Store it somewhere safe.\"",
      "shared": false
    },
    {
      "element": "Subtitle \"Choose a passphrase to lock the backup file.\"",
      "issue": "Rendered in primary teal at near-title size, so it looks like a tappable link and competes with the heading.",
      "fix": "Set `variant=\"bodyMedium\"` with `color: theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant`, margin 8px below the app bar area and 24px above the first field. Reserve `colors.primary` for interactive text only (add this as the default for the shared ScreenHeader subtitle prop).",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Tab bar active/inactive colors",
      "issue": "\"Settings\" renders in blue while the other items are teal — two different accent colors, neither clearly indicating the active tab.",
      "fix": "Set `tabBarActiveTintColor: theme.colors.primary`, `tabBarInactiveTintColor: theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant` in the shared navigator options and delete per-tab color overrides; ensure no raw hex blue remains in theme.ts.",
      "shared": true
    }
  ]
}

